# OpenWolf: machine-local state. Protocol: SHARDS.md (repo-owned, update-immune).
#
# Committed state (the shard protocol, 2026-09-18 cutover):
#   SHARDS.md, config.json, cerebrum/ (5 section files), STATUS.md (lean),
#   memory.md (frozen), token-ledger.json (frozen), buglog/ (per-session JSONL
#   shards — THE bug log), status/done/ (one file per milestone),
#   anatomy-seed.json (curated seed), hooks/ (frozen vendored stack) and tools/
#   (repo-owned shard tooling).
#
# Derived, machine-local — NEVER commit these (the "derived + committed" class
# caused every manual wolf merge in this repo's history):
#   buglog.json     rebuilt from buglog/ shards by wolf_bug.js rebuild (bootstrap)
#   anatomy.md      regenerated per machine by the post-write hook
#   anatomy-index.json   same
#
# Two deliberate deviations from the stock OpenWolf 2.5 ignore list (unchanged):
#
#   - hooks/ stays COMMITTED (fresh containers have no `openwolf` install — the
#     CLI is RETIRED here anyway; `git checkout -- .wolf` is the recovery path).
#   - token-ledger.json stays COMMITTED as a frozen history snapshot; new
#     telemetry is one session-ledgers/SESSION-<host>-<uuid>.json per session.
#
# Everything below is genuinely per-machine or per-session.
backups/
cache/
daemon.log
daemon.pid
dashboard-token
typesafe-api-key
_scan-state.json
*.lock
*.tmp
/buglog.json
/anatomy.md
/anatomy-index.json

# Hook runtime: per-session state and health heartbeats, not the scripts.
hooks/_*.json
hooks/sessions/
hooks/session-identities/
